   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"6\\left( {y - 2} \\right) - 5y = 4\\left( {y + 3} \\right) - 4\\left( {y - 1} \\right)\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 1: Simplify each side as much as possible.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"6y - 12 - 5y = 4y + 12 - 4y + 4\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y - 12 = 16\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: Collect the variable terms on one side.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y - 12 = 16\"></span></p>\n<p>There is nothing to do here.</p>\n<p>Step 3: Collect the constant terms on the other side.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y - 12 + 12 = 16 + 12\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y = 28\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 4: Make the coefficient of the variable term equal to 1.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y = 28\"></span></p>\n<p>You are already done. This is the solution.</p>\n<p>Step 5: Checking is left to you.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y = 28\">y = 28</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
